LOK: in the master view, a part's info is its master

In the master view getParts counts the masters and getPartName names
them, but getPartInfo still read the slide at the same index. With
more masters than slides the last parts had no page, so the info had
no "visible" and clients could not list the parts; below that, each
master carried its slide's visibility and size. Read the master page
in the master view, as getPartName does.

--- a/sd/source/ui/unoidl/unomodel.cxx
+++ b/sd/source/ui/unoidl/unomodel.cxx
@@ -4583,7 +4583,10 @@
     if (!pViewSh)
         return OUString();
 
-    SdPage* pSdPage = mpDoc->GetSdPage(nPart, pViewSh->GetPageKind());
+    // In the master view, parts are masters, as getParts counts.
+    SdPage* pSdPage = isMasterViewMode()
+                          ? mpDoc->GetMasterSdPage(nPart, PageKind::Standard)
+                          : mpDoc->GetSdPage(nPart, pViewSh->GetPageKind());
     const sal_Int16 nMasterPageCount= pViewSh->GetDoc()->GetMasterSdPageCount(pViewSh->GetPageKind());
 
     ::tools::JsonWriter jsonWriter;
